{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "provenance": "Hand-written by the platform team on 2026-10-28 from the mapping failures in docs/progress/GENERAL_PIPELINE_LOG.md and from deliberate near-opposite traps. Contains clinical expectations only: public ICD-9/ICD-10 code prefixes, drug ingredient names, and names of concepts already in config/mappings or config/variables. No MIMIC data.",
  "spec": "en: the English label a correct translation gives for a Chinese query (used as the simulated term expansion). right/trap: concept (a pack concept_id or variable definition_id: its identifiers), drug_class (a class_id of config/drug-classes: labels containing a member ingredient), label_contains (labels containing any of the words), label_pattern (a case-insensitive regular expression on the label), icd10 / icd9 (code prefixes; dots removed), icd_pattern (a regular expression on the code). An empty right means no dictionary entry is the right answer (the concept is a table field or a group).",
